This needs fixing before merge: the length is wrong for objects the multipart client stored in parts (over 8 MiB by default). It hands back part 1's response, so a 20 MiB obs reports 8388608 where master's HEAD gave 20971520, and legacyui's `ComplexObsServlet` sends that as Content-Length. S3Mock ignores `partNumber`, so the IT can't catch it.

```suggestion
		metadata.setLength(getObjectLength(getResponse));
		return new DataWithMetadata(response, metadata);
	}

	/**
	 * With multipart enabled the client downloads in parts and hands back the first part's response, so
	 * Content-Length is that part's size, while Content-Range ends with the size of the object.
	 */
	private Long getObjectLength(GetObjectResponse response) {
		String total = StringUtils.substringAfterLast(response.contentRange(), "/");
		return StringUtils.isNumeric(total) ? Long.valueOf(total) : response.contentLength();
	}
```

This needs fixing before merge: legacy obs with long non-ASCII titles stop loading. Pre-2.8 files are named `<title>_<uuid>.<ext>` ([source](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core/blob/df94143ec17c049ef0fc05cf6365593e6034efb1/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/obs/handler/AbstractHandler.java#L57-L72)), and `encodeKey` turns each non-ASCII byte into `%XX`, so a 36-letter Cyrillic title encodes past the 255-byte name limit. The stat then fails with "File name too long", not `NoSuchFileException`, so the legacy file is never tried:

```java
import java.nio.file.FileSystemException;

	private <T> T read(String key, IOFunction<Path, T> reader) throws IOException {
		Path path = storageDir.resolve(encodeKey(key));
		FileSystemException currentLocationFailure = null;
		if (isInStorageDir(path)) {
			try {
				return reader.apply(path);
			} catch (FileSystemException e) {
				// Not only a missing file: a legacy name the encoding pushes past the file system's name
				// length limit fails here too, so the legacy location decides
				currentLocationFailure = e;
			}
		}

		Path legacyPath = getLegacyStorageDir().resolve(key);
		if (fileExists(legacyPath)) {
			assertKeyInLegacyStorageDir(legacyPath, key);
			return reader.apply(legacyPath);
		}

		if (currentLocationFailure != null) {
			throw currentLocationFailure;
		}
		throw new IllegalArgumentException("Key must not point outside storage dir. Wrong key: " + key);
	}
```

Before merge this needs to reach the bundled handlers, which are what [TRUNK-6682](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/TRUNK-6682)'s call-count criterion guards. All five override `AbstractHandler.getObs`, so re-adding `storageService.exists(key)` to `BinaryStreamHandler`, or a separate `getMetadata` to `TextHandler`, leaves every test green. Each handler's test could run its own `getObs` against `CountingStorageService`, moved to its own file:

```java
TextHandler handler = new TextHandler();
ReflectionTestUtils.setField(handler, "adminService", adminService);
ReflectionTestUtils.setField(handler, "storageService", counting);
```

